<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Ash'karr biome names. Owner 2026-09-07, on reading the world map: "I see
       'Cypre Jungle' - I thought we were renaming all of this?" 30 distinct
       biomes are painted on the planet; only 4 carry our own defNames
       (RUT_TwilightSea, RUT_GreySea, RUT_NightsideIce, RUT_TheScald). The other
       26 show a donor's label even though every one of them already has a
       campaign name from its own biome sheet under
       design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/ - see BIOME_LABEL_CAMPAIGN_NAMES_1.

       The player never sees a defName, only <label>. So this is a label-only
       patch, same convention as CreatureNames_Ashkarr.xml and
       PlantNames_Ashkarr.xml: PatchOperationConditional guards each replace so
       a donor that is not installed simply produces a no-op, no MayRequire
       roster to maintain.

       🔴 LABEL ONLY. No defName is touched. Do not touch the tiles CSV.

       Two defs are claimed by more than one biome sheet - `Desert` and
       `ExtremeDesert` (the dune sea and the deep desert both paint
       `ExtremeDesert`, ruled R22 in _freeze_rulings_2026-09-07.md: the def is
       the binding unit, one merged roster obeying both sheets, no region
       split). A def has one label, so neither sheet's own regional name
       (`dune_sea.md`'s "the Dune Sea") can own it alone. `deep_desert.md`'s own
       title is already the higher-level term that spans both regions, so that
       is what is used here - "the Deep Desert" - and `desert.md`'s single-sheet
       name is used for `Desert` unchanged, "the Desert". These two are NOT
       spelled out in BIOME_LABEL_CAMPAIGN_NAMES_1's own table (only the
       collision rule is); confirm before treating as final.

       `SeaIce` (262 tiles) is claimed by no biome sheet - left untouched here,
       per the item's own note to decide that before labelling.

       BIOME_TEXT_PORT_1 (2026-09-11) added the three below: `Scarlands`,
       `Wasteland` and `AridShrubland` were never touched by this file at all
       (not an oversight of THIS list — they simply were not on the original
       30-biome sheet-name census) and so still showed lowercase donor labels
       ("scarlands", "wasteland", "arid shrubland") to the player. Their own
       RUT_ BiomeDefs (RUT_Scarlands, RUT_Wasteland, RUT_AridShrubland) already
       carry the correct campaign label; this only copies each onto the donor
       defName the tiles actually use, same conditional convention as every
       other row here. See BiomeDescriptions_Ashkarr.xml (same commit) for the
       matching description/settleWarning port — that file is the one that
       actually closes the 4 plot leaks; this one only fixes the label case. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MycoticJungle"]/label</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_MycoticJungle"]/label</xpath>
      <value><label>the Rot</label></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>   <!-- was "mycotic jungle" -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_PropaneLakes"]/label</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_PropaneLakes"]/label</xpath>
      <value><label>the Propane Lakes</label></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>   <!-- was "propane lakes" -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="BiomeGRimond"]/label</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="BiomeGRimond"]/label</xpath>
      <value><label>the Blue Desert</label></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>   <!-- was "Blue desert" -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_RockyCrags"]/label</xpath>
